{
  "name": "Claude Code + Desktop + All Observed Helpers — Code ID and Path Deny",
  "description": "Little Snitch 6; 23 rules: 16 Code ID rules for the 4 Anthropic identities observed via codesign (for each: allow Surge Fake-IP 198.18.0.0/15, IPv4 127.0.0.0/8, IPv6 ::1/128, deny other outgoing); plus 7 exact executable-path deny-any fallbacks for Claude Code installed via Homebrew Cask 2.1.323 and the 6 observed Claude Desktop executables including 4 Helpers and iOS Sim. PATH FALLBACKS: no address allow is added for paths; this is intentional to avoid granting additional access if another program is substituted at one of these paths. With same regular priority, Code ID address-specific allow outranks path deny-any. A path deny will only protect an altered binary if its process identification still matches: inspect whether Little Snitch enables a path code-identity check. .lsrules does not document setting the path identity-check mode. Paths are exact, NOT recursive and NOT upgrade-stable. No homebrew symlink path (/opt/homebrew/bin/claude) because it was marked ineffective in Little Snitch. Remote subscription may disable new allow rules. Check all enabled and applied, including process-via-helper attribution, in Network Monitor. Demo Mode and external helper subprocesses remain risks.",
